    // Single scattering alone underestimates a clear sky by roughly a factor of\r
    // three, and it underestimates blue the most, because a blue photon is the\r
    // one most likely to scatter again rather than to be absorbed. Left\r
    // uncorrected the sky is too dim to fill shadows, the warm ground bounce\r
    // wins the ambient, and snow shadows come out beige instead of blue — which\r
    // is the opposite of the whole look.\r
