    // them black. Omitting it — as a naive sky model does — is precisely why\r
    // untuned snow renders come out with dead, crushed shadows.\r
    //\r
    // The handover has to be *fast* — one and a half degrees either side of\r
    // where the clip actually begins. Run it any wider and the band below the\r
    // horizon holds mostly the clipped march, which is dark for an artefactual\r
    // reason: a ray angled into the planet is cut short, accumulates almost no\r
    // single scattering, and single scattering is all this integral has. That\r
    // leaves a dark stripe in the LUT exactly where the ground meets the sky,\r
